From 2f437340d2929408a14509530a8e462198bb9caf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:57:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] boss, http: Akamai SpotPass URLs, skip uploads, boss:P
 sessions

- SpotPass URLs wrapped by Akamai
  (https://a248.e.akamai.net/f/248/103046/10m/npdl.c.app.nintendowifi.net/p01/...,
  used by the eShop's BGM tasks) are recognised and redirected to the
  custom SpotPass server like the direct Nintendo addresses.
  X-Tangelo-Original-Host carries the wrapped Nintendo host.
- Upload tasks (npul, /p01/recv/, e.g. Miiverse) are no longer
  downloaded with GET: they're reported as failed without a request,
  and not started at session start.
- boss:P InitializeSessionPrivileged creates the session like
  InitializeSession, so the HOME Menu's task and property calls after
  it work instead of failing with "uninitialized BOSS session".
- boss:P GetOptoutFlagPrivileged (0x0407) and GetStorageInfoPrivileged
  (0x044D) read the title's opt-out flag and storage size from BOSS_A.db.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
